t inside the last decade. So I widen right rather than compress it: sigma_right 0.80, sigma_left 0.95 (full unconditional recession width retained, since a five-year window containing one synchronized recession is the modal historical experience). P10 = 1.95 - 1.282(0.95) = 0.73 -> 0.75. P90 = 1.95 + 1.282(0.80) = 2.98 -> 3.00. THE MODEL: I adopt nothing from it except the PPP weights. Two seats verified independently that src/modules/production.ts sets gamma = 0.55 on useful energy against a mainstream cost-share 0.05-0.08 the repository itself flags, that a grep of src/modules/ returns no termPremium, no nominal sovereign benchmark and no unemployment field, and that its region proxy (us + oecd-ex-us + china) places Japan, Korea and Turkiye outside the OECD leg — i.e. it excludes the two best-matched aging economies on earth while its energy channel carries the growth. Its 2.95-3.90% coupled prints are biased up in two compounding ways and are uninformative about CQ3.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:58.542Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"The NY Fed ACM or Kim-Wright US 10y real term premium prints BELOW +0.40% as a trailing twelve-month average WHILE the real 10s30s slope (DFII30 minus DFII10) flattens to under +15bp, with no new G7 purchase programme, buyback expansion, SLR recalibration or statutory captive-demand mandate announced in the interim.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the ONE piece of evidence my CQ4 level rests on — the 2.5:1 multi-sovereign duration-repricing signal — without the repression explanation that would otherwise save me. It would mean 2026 was a transient selloff of the 2013-14 type. CQ4 P50 falls ~40bp to ~1.10% and the distribution loses its right skew (P90 to ~2.2%); CQ5 falls from 19 to ~12; CQ6-C falls ~5pp and CQ6-D rises ~4pp; CQ3 essentially unaffected, since my growth answer rests on demographic arithmetic rather than on the yield.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"FRED DFII10 twelve-month trailing average >= 2.75% AND G7 GDP-weighted 10y real yield (nominal benchmark minus 10y inflation swap) >= 2.40% on a trailing-twelve-month basis, with no material repression measure enacted in any G7 sovereign on my tighter definition (>= 50bp of suppression sustained).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies BOTH my ~-45bp mean-reversion assumption and my 0.52 repression probability at once, and vindicates the Fermi/Scout seats I down-weighted. CQ4 P50 rises ~65bp to ~2.15% and P10 to ~1.20%; CQ5 rises from 19 to ~29 via the MOVE conjunct; CQ6-C rises ~6pp and CQ6-A falls ~5pp; CQ2's OECD conjunct falls ~4pp, since the inflation-tolerant wedge I priced would not be operating.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of >= 25% occurs AND G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yields rise >= 25bp (or fail to fall 50bp) inside the drawdown window.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my central reconciliation on CQ5's second conjunct — that a capex-bust drawdown is disinflationary and bond-bullish (2000-02, 2007-09, Japan 1989-92), which is where I moved toward the red-team and away from Wave 1's 2022 template. CQ5's conjunct B resolves YES on its own, so CQ5 collapses to conjunct A and rises from 19 to ~33-36; CQ4 P90 fattens toward 3.1 and P50 rises ~25bp; CQ6-C rises ~5pp at D's expense.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Realized PPP-weighted real GDP growth for OECD-38 + China over 2027-2031 (IMF WEO / OECD Economic Outlook, constant-PPP aggregation) comes in at or below 1.55%/yr, with China's own 2029-2031 average below 2.5%.\",\"by_when\":\"Jun 30, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my partial acceptance of the red-team's double-subtraction correction — it would mean the locked 2A coefficients ARE counterfactual-net and the Wave-1 seats were